.TH UNIQ 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
uniq \- report or filter out repeated lines in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uniq
.RB [ \-c | \-d | \-u ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR fields ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR chars ]
.RI [ input_file
.RI [ output_file ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uniq
reads
.I input_file
(or standard input, if omitted or given as
.BR \- )
one line at a time and writes it to
.I output_file
(or standard output, if omitted or given as
.BR \- ),
collapsing each run of
.B adjacent
equal lines into a single output line. Only immediately-adjacent
lines are ever compared;
.B uniq
never sorts its input, so a caller wanting duplicates collapsed
regardless of position should sort the input first.
.PP
Comparison is an exact byte comparison, after skipping any prefix
named by
.B \-f
and/or
.BR \-s ;
there is no case-insensitive comparison mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Precede each output line with the number of lines in its input run
that compared equal, right-justified in a 7-character field followed
by a space.
.TP
.B \-d
Write only the first line of each run that occurred more than once
(i.e., only actual duplicates).
.TP
.B \-u
Write only lines that occurred exactly once (i.e., were never
duplicated).
.RS
.PP
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-d ,
and
.B \-u
are mutually exclusive; giving more than one is an error.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-f " fields"
Ignore the first
.I fields
fields (each field being a run of <blank> characters followed by a
run of non-<blank> characters) when comparing lines. If a line has
fewer than
.I fields
fields, comparison starts from the end of the line (an empty
remainder).
.TP
.BI \-s " chars"
Ignore the first
.I chars
characters after the
.B \-f
skip (or from the beginning of the line, if
.B \-f
is not given) when comparing lines. If fewer than
.I chars
characters remain, comparison starts from the end of the line.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I input_file
The pathname of the file to read, or
.B \-
for standard input.
.TP
.I output_file
The pathname of the file to write, or
.B \-
for standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The input was processed successfully.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred: an invalid option or option argument, conflicting
.BR \-c / \-d / \-u ,
too many operands, an unreadable input file, or an unwritable output
file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sort (1),
.BR comm (1)
